{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "paraphrase:693c559e842aadf93ddcaba5f140c97aac1419c23fda3c1038c7a690c13b1213", "sample_idx": 28, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Section 1\nThe Guardian newspaper has issued corrections to several articles published on August 25th. These corrections address inaccuracies related to various topics, ranging from legal matters to biographical details and historical events. The newspaper is committed to accuracy and has promptly addressed these errors to ensure its readers receive reliable information. The corrections highlight the importance of careful fact-checking in journalism and the ongoing process of refining published content.\n\n***\n\nSection 2\nOne correction clarifies the geographical scope of a new pet theft law, stating it applies specifically to England and Northern Ireland, not the entire UK. Another addresses a misattribution of the title \"founder\" of Fertifa, clarifying that Eileen Burbidge is the executive director, while Tony Chen and Nick Kuan are the company's founders. Furthermore, the newspaper corrected a reference to the ethnicity of the family featured in the film *Bend It Like Beckham*, stating they are Sikh, not Muslim.\n\nSection 3\n* An article concerning pet theft law was corrected to specify its applicability to England and Northern Ireland.\n* A biographical error regarding Fertifa's founders was rectified, clarifying Eileen Burbidge's role as executive director.\n\nSection 4\nThe corrections also include an adjustment to a statement about Venetia Stanley's father converting to Islam; it was her uncle who did so. Additionally, a correction was made regarding the arrest of Pavel Durov, clarifying the location of the reported arrest. Other articles that have been amended include stories about royal servants, Pope Francis' views on England's football team, Britain's potential as a sci-tech superpower, and the Salvator Mundi painting. Readers are encouraged to direct any further corrections or concerns to the Readers’ Editor via the provided contact information.\n\nP.P.S. The Observer values reader feedback and strives to maintain the highest standards of journalistic integrity.\n\n\n\nWrite to the Readers’ Editor, the Observer, York Way, London N1 9GU, email observer.readers@observer.co.uk, tel 020 3353 4736\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Section", "logprob": -0.00033802041434682906}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.3870837688446045}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -0.0902138277888298}, {"token": "▁Guardian", "logprob": -0.00886433757841587}, {"token": "▁newspaper", "logprob": -0.4346238076686859}, {"token": "▁has", "logprob": -0.02900678664445877}, {"token": "▁issued", "logprob": -0.04860788211226463}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.7335565090179443}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.0094505799934268}, {"token": "▁several", "logprob": -0.00016616393986623734}, {"token": "▁articles", "logprob": -0.04915846511721611}, {"token": "▁published", "logprob": -2.098061486321967e-05}, {"token": "▁on", "logprob": -0.0006113567505963147}, {"token": "▁August", "logprob": -7.366862701019272e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "5", "logprob": -3.576272320060525e-06}, {"token": "th", "logprob": -1.9073468138230965e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.012373351491987705}, {"token": "▁These", "logprob": -0.010432825423777103}, {"token": "▁corrections", "logprob": -0.12852957844734192}, {"token": "▁address", "logprob": -0.22837476432323456}, {"token": "▁inaccuracies", "logprob": -0.2701004445552826}, {"token": "▁related", "logprob": -1.9713040590286255}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "▁various", "logprob": -0.41190895438194275}, {"token": "▁topics", "logprob": -0.002494083484634757}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.04963444545865059}, {"token": "▁ranging", "logprob": -0.595969021320343}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": 